{
  "_readme": [
    "Framework labels for every lesson. Resolved at build time by",
    "scripts/build_site.py: a lesson takes its track's labels unless it appears",
    "in `lessons`, which replaces them entirely.",
    "",
    "These are INDICATIVE mappings, kept in one reviewable file so they can be",
    "argued with by pull request. They are the frameworks a lesson's risk and",
    "control speak to — not a certification, and not a claim that studying a",
    "lesson discharges an obligation.",
    "",
    "Vocabulary, deliberately narrow so nothing here is invented:",
    "  owasp  OWASP Agentic AI Top 10 threat ids (T1-T15) and OWASP Top 10 for",
    "         LLM Applications ids (LLM01-LLM10).",
    "  atlas  MITRE ATLAS. Tactic names are used rather than technique ids,",
    "         except AML.T0051 (LLM Prompt Injection), which is unambiguous.",
    "  nist   NIST AI RMF 1.0 core functions: GOVERN, MAP, MEASURE, MANAGE.",
    "  euai   EU AI Act (Regulation 2024/1689) article numbers.",
    "",
    "An empty list is a valid, explicit answer: A0 is a setup track and maps to",
    "no control. scripts/check_frameworks.py fails the build if any lesson",
    "resolves to nothing at all without its track declaring that on purpose.",
    "Every label links out. `urls` below holds the destinations, and",
    "scripts/check_framework_links.py fetches each one and fails on anything",
    "that is not a 200 — a label pointing at a dead page is worse than a label",
    "with no link, because a reader who clicks it stops trusting the rest.",
    "",
    "MITRE ATLAS links to the site root rather than to per-technique pages:",
    "atlas.mitre.org serves its deep paths from client-side routing and they",
    "could not be verified, and an unverifiable link is not shipped."
  ],
